 "critic": "Most cards suggest templates through interchangeable full names, fixed rewards, generic locations, and three-option menus. Several switch from third-person reporting into first-person speech. Paying a stranger's loss or clinic bill repeatedly appears beside investigation as though the actions were equivalent. Reputation and outsider explanations often feel appended. The Claws fees have a credible recurring cause, while Ivo's refusal, threatened escalation, and collective resistance connect particularly well. Injury causing missed work also feels natural, though the work itself often stays vague. Repeated wording and exact duplicates reinforced the impression of assembled parts. Night City specificity usually comes from Claws, ripperdocs, credsticks, and eddies rather than distinctive voices.",
